NAME
     klogd - put the kernel's messages into the log

SYNOPSIS
     klogd [-n]

DESCRIPTION
     klogd reads the kernel's message ring and hands what it finds to
     syslogd, so that what printk said is in /var/log/messages as well
     as in dmesg.

OPTIONS
     -n   stay in the foreground

SEE ALSO
     dmesg(1), syslogd(8)
